<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT - Coelba started.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - Coelba started.</headline>
<text>
<p>-- HSBC James Capel said it started coverage of Brazilian power distributor Companhia de Eletricidade de Bahia (Coelba) with a rating of long-term buy.</p>
<p>-- &quot;Coelba is scheduled to be the first distribution company in the developing northeast region of Brazil to be privatized,&quot; analyst Luciana Portolano wrote in a report. The sale is scheduled for August 1997.</p>
<p>-- &quot;The company has taken the initial steps toward becoming an efficient and profitable concessionaire, and operates in an area with above-average growth rates in electricity consumption.&quot;</p>
<p>-- Ian Simpson, Wall Street Desk (212) 859-1879</p>
